{"id":"a4","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":5,"of":16,"title":"The","titleHe":"יְדִיעָה","goal":"Use הַ, and know why it sometimes becomes הָ.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"There is no word for a. סֵפֶר on its own means a book. To say the book you attach הַ to the front — it is part of the word, not a separate one."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"סֵפֶר → הַסֵּפֶר","en":"a book → the book"},{"he":"יֶלֶד → הַיֶּלֶד","en":"a boy → the boy"},{"he":"בַּיִת → הַבַּיִת","en":"a house → the house"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Before א ה ח ע ר, the הַ lengthens to הָ, because those letters can't take the doubling dot that normally follows: הָאִישׁ the man, הָעִיר the city, הָרֹאשׁ the head."}],"vocab":[{"he":"הַסֵּפֶר","en":"the book","translit":"hasefer"},{"he":"הָאִישׁ","en":"the man","translit":"ha'ish"},{"he":"הָעִיר","en":"the city","translit":"ha'ir"},{"he":"הַיּוֹם","en":"today, the day","translit":"hayom"},{"he":"הַכֹּל","en":"everything","translit":"hakol"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["the book","family","his","children"],"correct":0,"prompt":"הַסֵּפֶר","translit":"hasefer"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["flower","the man","nice","cat"],"correct":1,"prompt":"הָאִישׁ","translit":"ha'ish"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["the city","fear","when (literary)","certainly"],"correct":0,"prompt":"הָעִיר","translit":"ha'ir"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["hair","today, the day","discount","him, it"],"correct":1,"prompt":"הַיּוֹם","translit":"hayom"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["idea","mouse","to the right","everything"],"correct":3,"prompt":"הַכֹּל","translit":"hakol"},{"type":"read","he":"הָאִישׁ","translit":"ha'ish","en":"the man"},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"סֵפֶר → ___","en":"a book → the book","options":["הַיּוֹם","הַסֵּפֶר","הָאִישׁ","הָעִיר"],"correct":1,"full":"סֵפֶר → הַסֵּפֶר"},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"בַּיִת → ___","en":"a house → the house","options":["הַסֵּפֶר","הַיּוֹם","הָאִישׁ","הַבַּיִת"],"correct":3,"full":"בַּיִת → הַבַּיִת"},{"type":"choice","q":"Why is it הָעִיר and not הַעִיר?","options":["ע can't take the doubling dot, so the vowel lengthens","עִיר is feminine","It's an exception with no reason","Because the word is plural"],"correct":0},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “everything”?","options":["הַתְחָלָה","קְצָת","הַכֹּל","חַג"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “today, the day”?","options":["הַיּוֹם","אוֹכֵל","זוֹל","פְּרִי"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Which is “the country”?","options":["הָאָרֶץ","הַאָרֶץ","אָרֶץ הַ","הָאֶרֶץ הַ"],"correct":0,"why":"אֶרֶץ starts with א, so the article is הָ — and the noun's own vowel shifts: הָאָרֶץ."},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["הָאִישׁ","הַיּוֹם","הָעִיר","הַכֹּל"],"correct":0,"say":"הָאִישׁ","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “the man”?","options":["הָאִישׁ","כֹּהֵן","כְּאֵב","חֶסֶד"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["הַסֵּפֶר","the book"],["הָאִישׁ","the man"],["הָעִיר","the city"],["הַיּוֹם","today, the day"],["הַכֹּל","everything"]]},{"type":"type","q":"Write “the book” in Hebrew","answer":"הַסֵּפֶר","hint":"hasefer"}]}